---
import PageHeading from '../../components/ui/PageHeading.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Architecture governance"
  description="How MailFlow architecture decisions are proposed, changed, superseded, and audited."
  currentPath="/governance/"
>
  <div class="content-wrap" data-pagefind-body>
    <PageHeading
      eyebrow="Change is a traced transaction"
      title="Governance"
      description="The baseline remains active narrative authority. Catalogs and diagrams are maintained projections. A material architecture change requires human approval and synchronized evidence."
    />
    <section class="record-panel">
      <h2>Completion gate</h2><p>
        An architecture change is complete only when all six conditions hold:
      </p><ol>
        <li>The applicable baseline is updated.</li><li>Descriptive content is updated.</li><li>
          Affected diagrams are updated.
        </li><li>Related decisions are updated.</li><li>
          The applicable ADR or changelog is updated.
        </li><li>Coverage tests pass.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="record-panel">
      <h2>Change workflow</h2><ol>
        <li>Open an impact review using the repository template.</li><li>
          Locate affected source ranges and stable IDs.
        </li><li>Record a new decision, a decision change, or an explicit supersession.</li><li>
          Update the active baseline after human approval.
        </li><li>Refresh structured projections, topology, descriptive pages, and ADR.</li><li>
          Run integrity, coverage, links, accessibility, E2E, build, and privacy gates.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="record-panel">
      <h2>Stable identity</h2><p>
        Decision, service, stack, gate, diagram, relationship, trust-boundary, section, and block
        IDs are presentation-independent. A decision never lives only inside a component, and a
        visual component never redefines it.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="record-panel">
      <h2>Working material</h2><ul class="record-links">
        <li><a href="/coverage/">Coverage report</a></li><li>
          <a href="/decisions/">Decision catalog</a>
        </li><li><a href="/gates/">Validation gates</a></li><li>
          <a href="/explorer/">Diagram explorer</a>
        </li>
      </ul><p>
        Repository templates live in <code>docs/templates/</code>; ADR guidance and template live in <code
          >docs/adr/</code
        >. Private commercial documents remain in <code>docs/client/</code> and are excluded from the
        public build.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
